  "summary_md": "Consumer discretionary spending remains uneven across specialty retail, but today’s batch is defined by a wave of profitability milestones and balance-sheet repair. EVGO delivered its first quarter of positive adjusted EBITDA and secured a critical DOE loan amendment, cementing an infrastructure-growth narrative. BNED’s campus-bookstore turnaround reached an inflection point with a newly declared dividend and an upcoming Investor Day, while QNST’s AI‑powered platform and HomeBuddy acquisition continue to drive record top‑line momentum. The ad agency names are pivoting hard to digital—EVC’s Smadex platform and TSQ’s local‑market model reflect that shift. Less reassuringly, TULP booked a sharp margin collapse with no accompanying commentary, making it the morning’s most opaque report. Across the board, capital allocation is tilting toward buybacks (BARK) and dividends (BNED, NCMI), suggesting management teams are prioritizing profit conversion and shareholder returns after a prolonged restructuring cycle.",
